  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for the return of displaced populations and host populations in Bria commune, Haute Kotto prefecture in the Central African Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The sub-prefecture of Bria in the Central African Republic has been affected by armed and community conflicts which led to the displacement of 55,698 people (CMP 30 October 2022). Among these displaced, 20,908 are housed with host families and 34,790 occupy displacement sites, mainly the Point Kilometer 03 (PK03) site. Through this project, IOM aims to support the returns identified in the prefecture of Haute Kotto/sub-prefecture of Bria, by addressing the basic needs of the populations returned or intending to leave the site of displaced persons of PK03. The project is supporting returnee households through the reconstruction/rehabilitation of their shelters according to the standards of the Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) / the Shelter/ Non-Food Items (NFI) cluster and the provision of an NFI kit. Awareness-raising campaigns are also organized to promote ownership of the approach by communities of return. The project also has a Water, Hygiene and Sanitation (WASH) component that complements current and future actions by substantially improving access to drinking water and latrines in particularly disadvantaged neighbourhoods.</narrative>
  </description>
